+The CPU FM TX RAM interface is implemented as `hrc7000_fm_tx_audio`: capture FM_ADDR_SW b1:0 at the system
+interrupt, write the named half (1 low, 2 high), 256 signed samples with the high byte at the lower address.
+Selectors 0 and 3 are invalid. `hrc7000_fm_tx_audio_irq` enables SYS_INTERP b15 without changing other mask bits.
+The DMR engine dispatches `fm_tx` for that bit even while stopped; `hrc_dmr_fm_tx_hook` keeps the system IRQ active
+independently of the receive hook. Disable the mask and remove the hook before retiring its PCM source. Initialize
+both halves before selecting TX RAM, keep ring play off, and allow up to 64 ms of hardware playout after the
+software queue empties. A cancellation still stops immediately. Transport tests verify byte order, half boundaries,
+mask preservation and stopped-engine dispatch; deviation and filtering require measurements on each board.
+
 The FM transmit limiter (FM_DEV_COEF b23:16) caps the deviation of audio that enters through the codec ADC, the
 microphone and the mixer route below. The prompt FIFO's ring play is not capped by it: AFSK through
